WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:01.179
Hey, Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.179 --> 00:00:06.519
The world can be a confusing place sometimes
so, often, many of us try to make sense of

00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:11.120
it with our own little routines and rituals,
like always putting on your right shoe first

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.220
or locking the door three times to make sure
you don’t forget.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:21.039
But the amazing thing is how often these habits
and ideas become a full blown superstition,

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:23.460
some of which last for centuries.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.840
So cross your fingers, don’t step on the
cracks, throw some salt over your shoulder

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.680
and let’s go look at superstitions from
around the world.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.410
Let’s start in Asia.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.260
The first thing that jumps out is numbers.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.200
In China, 8 is considered lucky, since it
sounds like their word for prosperity.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.520
They really tried to get the most out of it
for the Olympics in Beijing by starting the

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:59.040
opening ceremony at 8 seconds and 8 minutes
past 8pm on 8th August 2008.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.250
By a strange coincidence, in Japan, it also
has the meaning of growing prosperous but

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.680
this is because the character for the number
8 (八 hachi) broadens gradually.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.750
By that logic, in English, 8 would mean you’re
going to become a snowman.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:18.630
But cut that eight in half and you have the
horrible number 4.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:25.200
Most of Eastern Asia is tetraphobic, meaning
they are scared of 4, due to its similarity

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.370
to the word for death.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:32.790
This is extremely widespread and you’re
unlikely to find buildings with a 4th floor,

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:37.780
goods sold in four-packs or any parking lots
with that digit.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:45.220
Even numbers like 14 and 24 or ones in their
40s are avoided, excluding 42 of course, I

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.860
may have just lost China.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:51.420
It’s so severe in fact that giving something
to a fellow Asian with the number four in

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:57.640
it can be enough for the police to get involved
since it’s seen as a death threat.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.720
So if you’re ever thinking about buying
property there, guess which house is going

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.360
to give you the sweetest deal?

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:11.039
India has an aversion to rounded numbers such
as 100 or 70, and prices are normally taken

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:16.189
up by one rupee to avoid them, a smart bit
of business.

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:22.769
Indians also like to feed milk to snakes,
usually as a religious offering.

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:28.019
Snakes don’t actually drink milk so thousands
die every year due to this practise.

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:30.579
So don’t feed snakes milk.

00:02:30.579 --> 00:02:36.549
Also, in Korea, don’t feed your boyfriend
chicken wings as it’s a sign that he will

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:39.249
fly away and leave you.

00:02:39.249 --> 00:02:43.220
Whereas in the west, if your partner feeds
you chicken wings it’s usually seen as a

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.959
sign that they’re a keeper.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:50.559
If you’re eating in Japan however, don’t
leave your chopsticks stuck in the rice as

00:02:50.559 --> 00:02:55.870
this is reserved for funerals, instead you
should rest them horizontally across the bowl.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.669
If you are at a funeral though, remember to
hide your thumbs or the recently departed

00:03:00.669 --> 00:03:06.660
will sneak under your nails and cause your
loved ones to die young, that’s if they

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.019
haven’t already been killed by leaving a
fan on whilst they sleep.

00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:18.129
Fan death is a very prevalent fear in South
Korea and all fans are sold with a “life-saving”

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:24.870
cut-off timer to prevent you being either
asphyxiated, frozen or boiled to death, depending

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.079
on which bit of air conditioning logic you
apply.

00:03:28.079 --> 00:03:32.090
No one knows how it all started but there
is an excellent conspiracy theory that the

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:36.389
government made it up during the 1970s energy
crisis.

00:03:36.389 --> 00:03:41.620
It would be like combating the California
drought by telling everyone that having a

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.969
bath makes you fat.

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:49.890
The Middle East has some of the oldest culture
that exists today so they have a rich tapestry

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.729
of myths and legends.

00:03:51.729 --> 00:03:54.709
One very common one is the evil eye.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:04:00.109
This is a curse than can bring great misfortune
to a person, giving them bad luck, an unhappy

00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:05.230
life, or perhaps just a bad dinner or no phone
reception, in very mild cases.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:10.949
The evil eye can get you at any time, cast
by a hate-filled glare without your knowing.

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:13.900
So how do you protect yourself from this terror?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:19.609
What you need is a Nazar; an eye shaped amulet,
typically a blue coloured crystal, that can

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:25.020
be worn around your neck, hung above your
door or lost down the back of your sofa.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:30.300
For non-amulet based protection, you can also
use the phrase “mashallah” which expresses

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.770
appreciation and you can try to dress yourself
humbly to avoid the eye’s vicious gaze.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:44.289
There is a universal protection against all
malicious spirits, not just eye based, called

00:04:44.289 --> 00:04:48.819
the Khamsa and it’s just an image of an
open right palm.

00:04:48.819 --> 00:04:54.300
Occasionally precious possessions such as
cars are anointed with right hand prints to

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.310
make sure they are protected.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:00.220
There are many superstitions based around
creepy crawlies.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:06.379
In Qatar, it was once believed that spiders
had the ability to control house fires so

00:05:06.379 --> 00:05:09.780
if you killed one, it was like murdering a
tiny firefighter.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.580
The spiders were no help at getting cats out
of trees though so fortunately they kept the

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.169
fire department up and running.

00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:22.990
Also beetles were a sign that guests are coming
and you should prepare for their arrival.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.970
Welcoming guests and people in need into your
home is actually a big part of Islamic culture.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:33.199
But they must be careful with their feet,
and not just to avoid crushing your eight-legged

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.289
firemen.

00:05:34.289 --> 00:05:40.419
A new home must be entered with the right
foot but a bathroom must be entered with the

00:05:40.419 --> 00:05:41.419
left.

00:05:41.419 --> 00:05:44.030
It’s the household hokey-cokey.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:50.009
In some areas of Africa, superstitions carry
a lot of weight and are a big part of daily

00:05:50.009 --> 00:05:54.970
life, especially when it comes to things like
sickness and success.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:59.310
Many villages across the continent have a
witch doctor, who will be consulted before

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.969
consulting a medical professional.

00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:07.680
Some of the cures that are suggested involve
the patient acquiring ingredients such as

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.629
the eggs of a snake or the claws of a wild
cat.

00:06:11.629 --> 00:06:16.270
I imagine it reduces the amount of people
calling in sick for work, imagine if you needed

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:20.129
to go get some alligator teeth in order to
be written a sick note…um…

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:23.009
no thanks, I’ll be at my desk.

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:29.860
In Sierra Leone, Alhaji Suliaman Kabba runs
the union of traditional healers and one major

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.669
area of concern for them are Witch Guns.

00:06:33.669 --> 00:06:38.370
These aren’t pointy hatted women holding
firearms like you might be thinking, but a

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.889
way of killing with a curse.

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:46.719
According to Kabba “the earliest and deadliest
type of witch gun is made out of the husk

00:06:46.719 --> 00:06:52.610
from rice” so beware anyone carrying a bag
of basmati through the airport check in.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.419
Although you don’t need to be on the plane
to do the damage, since the range of these

00:06:56.419 --> 00:06:58.139
guns is unlimited.

00:06:58.139 --> 00:07:03.810
And although witchcraft is not officially
recognised in the courts, suspects have still

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:09.639
been tried and convicted for these suspicious
killings nevertheless.

00:07:09.639 --> 00:07:14.720
Anyone who dies young without an obvious cause
is often thought to be a victim of a witch

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:15.720
gun attack.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:22.169
And if you can’t find a witch’s gun, then
grab her broomstick, since in Nigeria, it’s

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:28.289
thought that hitting a man with a broom can
cause him to becomes impotent, even making

00:07:28.289 --> 00:07:31.199
his entire genitals disappear.

00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:37.120
Fortunately, the victim can quickly save himself
if he grabs the broom and returns at least

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.069
seven blows to his attacker.

00:07:39.069 --> 00:07:44.249
I don’t even want to think about what happens
if you hit someone with a vacuum cleaner.

00:07:44.249 --> 00:07:49.849
Speaking of manhood, in order to reach it
within the Maasai tribe in Kenya, the young

00:07:49.849 --> 00:07:57.009
boy must head out to the plains and catch
himself a lion, using only a spear.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:08:03.050
We come to Europe now and we’ll start with
one of the favourite pastimes; drinking.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.849
From Russian vodka, to German beer and French
wine, the Europeans love to drink.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:14.159
A report from the World Health Organisation,
published in 2014, showed Belarus leading

00:08:14.159 --> 00:08:20.370
the world in alcohol consumption per capita
– with 17.5 litres of alcohol drunk per

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.199
person per year.

00:08:22.199 --> 00:08:27.370
Just to be clear, that’s pure booze, so
in more realistic terms, that would be equivalent

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.949
to about 900 pints of beer, per person, per
year.

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:41.140
In fact, European countries occupy 26 of the
top 30 alcohol consuming nations, with only

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:47.430
Grenada, South Korea, Australia and South
Africa joining in for another round at the

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.430
winner’s bar.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:54.260
So, given Europe’s love of the bottle, there
are plenty of alcoholic superstitions going

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.260
around.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.150
In Russia, you should always finish all of
your drink and if it’s a shot, you must

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:03.529
never put it back on the table until it is
empty.

00:09:03.529 --> 00:09:08.579
You should clink glasses for each new round
of drinks, unless you’re at a funeral.

00:09:08.579 --> 00:09:14.450
If you want to send your friends to their
funeral in Germany, you just have to say cheers,

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.820
or “prost” in German, with a glass of
water.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:24.110
It’s considered very rude in places like
Bavaria, since you are wishing death upon

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:25.110
everyone.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:29.720
But the Germans often meet up for a drink
down their local, often called a Stammtisch

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.510
– meaning regular’s table.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:37.730
When you walk in, rather than waving to the
group, you should knock on the oak table that

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:39.160
they are sitting around.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:45.310
Now, as you all know, the devil can’t touch
oak, he has some sort of allergy I believe.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.220
So, to prove you are not the devil, you should
rap on the table.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:53.860
In France, if you are drinking, you are likely
to be eating too.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:59.360
They have the generic fear of the number 13,
like much or Europe and the US, but it’s

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.420
especially true for a dinner party.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:09.070
Thirteen guests will mean things turn out
very badly for one unlucky diner.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:14.100
This is thought to come from Jesus’ last
supper, where Judas turned out to be a traitor.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:19.480
Any bread on the table should always be the
right way up, since upside down bread is the

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.980
bread for the hangman.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:27.459
In olden France, the bakers didn’t want
to serve the hangmen but the king warned them

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:31.920
that it was either that or they would end
up as toast themselves.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:37.149
So they picked out the worst bread and turned
it upside down, in disdain for their least

00:10:37.149 --> 00:10:38.930
popular customers.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:44.410
In Denmark, if your dinner party gets drunk
and disorderly and you end up breaking all

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:49.550
the crockery, not to worry, just scrape it
up and save it for the end of December.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:54.410
On New Year’s Eve, take all your smashed
plates and cups and chuck them at your friend’s

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.959
house as a way to break in the New Year.

00:10:56.959 --> 00:11:01.570
According to the Danes the more you pelt them
with, the better their next twelve months

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.250
will be.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:09.050
South America has the world’s largest jungle
and river; the Amazon and, as you can imagine

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:13.610
in a place with such a wild abundance of life,
the plants and animals have given rise to

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.680
a huge amount of different stories and beliefs.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:23.320
In Brazil, the river dolphins, or Boto, have
a mystical place in society.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.949
Anyone lost amongst the trees is thought to
have been taken into the water and turned

00:11:27.949 --> 00:11:29.610
into a dolphin.

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:37.100
They can’t turn back to human but they can
sneak onto the land, wearing catfish for shoes

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:42.880
and stingrays for hats, and impregnate the
local women.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:49.610
In Argentina, no one turns into a dolphin
but if you are foolish, and fertile enough,

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:52.600
to have a seventh son; beware.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.569
He will turn into a werewolf.

00:11:54.569 --> 00:12:02.660
And it won’t be every full moon that he
changes, rather every Tuesday and Friday specifically,

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.800
so he’ll never be able to join that yoga
class.

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:14.360
If you want to un-werewolf him, you’ll need
to get the president to adopt him.

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:18.709
One president who will be of no help though
is Carlos Menem.

00:12:18.709 --> 00:12:25.709
The Argentine leader throughout the 90s, his
name is now a curse, so avoid saying it in

00:12:25.709 --> 00:12:26.709
public.

00:12:26.709 --> 00:12:30.170
In Venezuela, it’s the Jaguars that are
bad luck and you must kill any that you see

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:32.009
lurking around the village.

00:12:32.009 --> 00:12:36.670
For good luck though, many South Americans
have a great way of wishing in the New Year.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:39.279
The key is yellow underwear.

00:12:39.279 --> 00:12:43.360
Nothing like a little splash of colour to
get you going for the next 6 months.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:49.209
However in Chile, beware of the splash, for
if a woman gets her dress wet while she is

00:12:49.209 --> 00:12:53.230
washing the clothes, she will end up with
a drunk husband.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:59.760
Now the US in particular, given its history,
is really a melting pot of superstitions from

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:00.820
around the world.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:07.449
So, there are some obvious ones that we all
know about but do you know how they came about?

00:13:07.449 --> 00:13:11.009
Many people have paraskevi…

00:13:11.009 --> 00:13:12.440
paraskevidiki…

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:15.960
they have this (onscreen – paraskevidekatriaphobia)
It’s a fear of Friday the 13th.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:21.170
Now it’s quite a new superstition, but certainly
older then Sean S Cunningham’s movie from

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.170
1980.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:26.819
It’s probably been around for a couple of
hundred years and is just a combination of

00:13:26.819 --> 00:13:32.500
a long held distrust of the number 13 and
the fact that Friday is the day Jesus was

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.190
crucified, so not his best day.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:40.399
Many superstitions such as this one, start
small but spread through a psychological reaction

00:13:40.399 --> 00:13:46.680
called the Baader-Meinhof phenomenon, sometimes
called frequency illusion.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:51.730
Say you meet someone at a party and they tell
you about this old band that they love, which

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:55.709
you’ve never heard of, let’s call them
Superdrive, for example.

00:13:55.709 --> 00:14:00.740
Then, the next day, you’re on a train, possibly
hungover thanks to the party, and you see

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:04.740
a guy wearing a t-shirt with Superdrive written
on it.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.630
Is the universe speaking to you?

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:09.839
Is this all an illusion and you’re the star
of your own Truman show?

00:14:09.839 --> 00:14:13.170
Are Superdrive investing in a crazy marketing
promotion?

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.540
Or just a glitch in the Matrix perhaps?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.759
No, it’s none of this.

00:14:17.759 --> 00:14:21.680
The world is full of a vast, unmanageable
amount of data.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:24.949
You can barely process a tiny fraction of
it.

00:14:24.949 --> 00:14:29.399
But what your brain does do incredibly well
is spot patterns and connections.

00:14:29.399 --> 00:14:34.310
That’s why you can recognise faces from
different angles and read words that are spelt

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.480
incorrectly.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:40.420
So when you have some new information, your
brain keeps an eye out for anything related

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.600
to it.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:47.170
If you’d seen that t-shirt a day before
or a week or two after, you wouldn’t have

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.980
even noticed.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:53.240
You only noticed it because your friend had
told you about the band the day before.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.240
This is known as the Baader-Meinhof phenomenon.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.139
So how does this relate to superstition?

00:14:57.139 --> 00:15:02.069
Well once you think something is unlucky,
like a certain date, you will immediately

00:15:02.069 --> 00:15:06.769
remember anything bad that happens to you
and associate it with that day.

00:15:06.769 --> 00:15:12.879
So if your date cancels on you on Friday 13th,
it’s all the calendars fault, but if you

00:15:12.879 --> 00:15:18.009
spill coffee on yourself on Saturday 14th,
it’s because you are a badly coordinated

00:15:18.009 --> 00:15:19.190
moron.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:25.920
Like Friday 13th, crossing your fingers is
also Christian in origin since anything with

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:29.250
the shape of the cross was considered a good
thing.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:35.029
And in fact, it could have started in a different
form, very early on in the history of Christianity.

00:15:35.029 --> 00:15:39.500
Now back in the day, around the time of the
Roman Empire, Christians were not exactly

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:43.560
everyone’s favourite and they would often
be sent off as a snack for the lions.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:49.000
So, in order to identify a fellow Christian,
there was a kind of secret handshake that

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.040
involved forming a cross with another’s
outstretched finger.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:59.410
And finally, probably one of the most common
superstitions around the world is that breaking

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:02.019
a mirror will bring you bad luck.

00:16:02.019 --> 00:16:06.010
This springs from the times of the Romans,
who were the first people to create glass

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.010
mirrors.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:11.579
It was thought that your reflection contained
a little piece of your soul so if the mirror

00:16:11.579 --> 00:16:17.279
broke, not only was your soul disfigured,
but it was also trapped in its shiny cage.

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:22.310
The association with seven years of bad luck,
is due to the Roman idea that your body renews

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:28.100
itself every seven years so you had to wait
it out till you grew whole again.

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:32.420
We all have our own ways of making sense of
the world and there’s nothing wrong with

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.199
the odd ritual and superstition to get you
through the day.

00:16:36.199 --> 00:16:40.980
But if you can’t leave the house without
wearing your lucky pants, carrying a horseshoe

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:45.860
and a rabbit’s foot, and breaking a wishbone
